Could you also add this same behavior for umarshalling errors + a testcase?

Also an idea for overall code improvement (probably better in a separate PR): Since this pattern of stopping on errors or recording and continuing occurs several times now throughout this loop, it might make sense to extract the single loop iteration into a separate method and then perform the error handling outside of it - something like:

```go
// testOne runs one query against one instance. It always returns a result.
// On failure, the result carries the error in Stats.Errors and err is non-nil.
func (qt *QueryTester) testOne(p testParams, grafanaInstance, link string) (model.QueryTestResult, error) {
...
}

link, err := GenerateExploreLink(...)
if err != nil {
	return nil, fmt.Errorf("error generating explore link: %v", err) // stays fatal
}
result, err := qt.testOne(params, grafanaInstance, link)
queryResults = append(queryResults, result)
if err != nil && !continueOnQueryTestingErrors {
	return queryResults, err
}
```
